    rdau:P61101 "<a href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicole_Hahn_Rafter'>Wikipedia</a>, katsottu 17.8.2026 (Nicole Hahn Rafter (1939–2016) was a feminist criminology professor at Northeastern University.)"@fi,
        "<a href='https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/bostonglobe/name/nicole-rafter-obituary?id=16805401'>Legacy</a>, katsottu 17.8.2026 (NICOLE RAFTER Obituary: RAFTER, Nicole Hahn (Nicky)[.] An internationally-known and much-honored writer and scholar in the fields of social history and criminology, the author of more than a dozen books (most recently The Crime of All Crimes, Toward a Criminology of Genocide), and a long-time professor at Northeastern University, passed away suddenly and unexpectedly, on February 29, 2016, at Beth Israel Deaconess Hospital in Boston. Nicky was 76 years old and lived in Boston's North End, where she was active in community affairs. )"@fi ;
